$NetBSD$

Use an md5 command that exists.

NetBSD's md5(1) prints only the digest, with no "MD5 (file) = " prefix and
no -r flag, so neither md5_darwin_freebsd.sh nor md5_openbsd.sh parses its
output; files/md5_netbsd.sh is added for it.

The genrule below is deliberately not given a netbsd arm.  The other BSDs
rewrite the packaging script's shebang to wherever their bash lives; there
is no bash here, so NetBSD falls to //conditions:default and the script is
copied with its #!/bin/bash intact.  That script is the self-extracting
installer's own, written in bash; pkgsrc installs output/bazel directly
and never runs it, so leaving it honestly marked as bash is better than
pointing it at a shell that will not run it or at a bash that is not
installed.

--- src/BUILD.orig	1980-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ src/BUILD
@@ -21,6 +21,8 @@ sh_binary(
     srcs = select({
         "//src/conditions:darwin": ["md5_darwin_freebsd.sh"],
         "//src/conditions:freebsd": ["md5_darwin_freebsd.sh"],
+        "//src/conditions:netbsd": ["md5_netbsd.sh"],
+        "//src/conditions:dragonfly": ["md5_darwin_freebsd.sh"],
         "//src/conditions:openbsd": ["md5_openbsd.sh"],
         "//conditions:default": ["md5_default.sh"],
     }),
